│ patch_name               │ complete_graph_symmetric_entangler                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the cube entangler with the complete eight-vertex graph, scheduled as seven       │
│                          │ disjoint perfect matchings. The current cube gives every qubit equal degree but still     │
│                          │ introduces an arbitrary coordinate system, whereas the binary pair features naturally     │
│                          │ describe edges between all qubit pairs. The complete CZ layer is invariant under every    │
│                          │ qubit permutation, so the full model better matches permutation-invariant record          │
│                          │ properties and should reduce sensitivity to vertex ordering. It also supplies global      │
│                          │ nonlinear interactions without adding trainable parameters, keeping the total at 26 and   │
│                          │ preserving the current parameter efficiency and low overfitting risk.                     │
