│ patch_description        │ This crossover merges the interspersed entanglement layering from the inspiration program │
│                          │ with the collective parameter sharing strategy of the current program. The inspiration    │
│                          │ model suffered from overfitting due to having independent parameters for every qubit in   │
│                          │ every layer, whereas the current program clumped all entangling gates together, which     │
│                          │ limited its expressiveness.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By inserting layers of parameterized, collectively-shared `RY` rotations between each     │
│                          │ dimensional grouping of the hypercube `CZ` gates, we significantly boost the              │
│                          │ expressiveness and entangling capability of each block. Because the parameters are shared │
│                          │ across all wires (vertex symmetry), the total parameter count remains extremely low (6    │
│                          │ per block). This provides strong regularization, matching the excellent generalization of │
│                          │ the current program while leveraging the superior architectural depth of the inspiration  │
│                          │ program.                                                                                  │
